  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Warm temperatures and breezy winds Sunday \nbefore the next rain chances early next week.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 1 DESCRIPTION...\nHigh pressure builds over the region Saturday and Saturday night\nbefore moving offshore Sunday. The remnants of Hurricane Isaias\nlift into the OH Valley on Sunday with moisture funneling up\ninto southern areas late Sunday night into Monday morning. \n\nBreezy southwest winds will also funnel warm temperatures into\nthe area Sunday into Monday. Highs will top out in the 60s both\ndays, some 3-8 degrees above normal. \n\nAs the system moves off the southern New England coast, it \ncould bring a chance of showers for the Downeast coast late Sunday\nnight into Monday. Rain chances could decrease if the system \nstays further south, though there is still a good amount of \nuncertainty at this time. A separate low pressure develops over \nthe Great Lakes Monday night as a trough deepens behind the \ndeparting tropical remnants. This will bring a chance of rain \nearly-mid next week.",
